WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.630
- J, where'd you grow up?

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.850
Where are you from originally?

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:11.190
- Originally, Ohio, Cincinnati.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.300
I was born and then ended
up in Indiana and in 2008

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.890
I ended up here in Skid Row.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.890
- Why did you come out here to Skid Row?

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.003
- Because there wasn't no
resources where I came from.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.513
I ran out of resources.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.220
The economy was low.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.220
And so I found this place
on the internet actually

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.250
and came out here with my tax returns.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.200
- Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.550
You had both your parents
growing up as a kid.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.550
- Yeah, it was a pretty typical family.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.540
I was well taken care of up
until about my teenage years,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.540
about 14 I moved out and it
was up and down since then.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.307
- How would you describe your childhood?

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.670
- Family-wise I was well taken care of

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:11.670
but growing up socially, it
was, I was very backward.

00:01:15.297 --> 00:01:17.950
I had a speech impediment,
a learning disability

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.580
also just being who, the
kind of person that I am a

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.680
I was always, pushed
aside or a zeroed out.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:37.050
- Was there a certain point
where you became transgender

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.673
or do you think you've
always been this way?

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.910
- Yeah, since I can remember, yeah.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.194
Kindergarden.

00:01:45.194 --> 00:01:46.027
- Correct.

00:01:46.027 --> 00:01:48.700
- So you always knew this
was your orientation?

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.000
- Yeah. Kindergarden I got
my first kiss on the leg

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.030
and butterflies, it's
been all downhill since.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:58.920
- It's been downhill?

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.200
- Yeah. Jokingly, but yeah.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.170
- And your life out here when I met you,

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.930
you were living on the street, right?

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:07.763
- Yeah.

00:02:07.763 --> 00:02:09.480
- When I met you about
seven, eight years ago

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.340
you were living on the street.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.950
- Yeah, I was there for seven years.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.113
I met somebody.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.690
He started running a
resource center, nonprofit

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.037
and I started it with him.

00:02:21.056 --> 00:02:22.160
- You have housing now?

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.360
You're you're in an apartment on Skid Row.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.103
- I got it in 2013.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.333
Has been quite horrid.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.467
I guess we don't realize it

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:38.360
but we become accustomed to some things.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:43.360
And ever since I got the
housing, it's been hard.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.240
cause I got so adjusted

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.750
to the outside and all
the activity around me.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:53.750
But so it's made it just
been a little harder.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.320
- That's interesting.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.490
So there's an adjustment from, to go

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.710
from living on the street
to living an apartment.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.543
- Yeah.

00:03:00.543 --> 00:03:03.130
I thought it would be
awesome, but it's been rough.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.520
- What was hard about that transition?

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.080
- Being alone.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.790
Just like spiritually,

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.040
I've been going through
a lot of things and-

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.210
- Yeah, the street life is very social.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.043
- Yeah.

00:03:14.043 --> 00:03:15.747
- There's people all over
the streets all the time.

00:03:15.747 --> 00:03:16.580
- Yeah.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.440
And you're always, there's
always some kind of

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.970
you're always looking
around, there's always

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.930
something's stimulating
but once you get inside

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.460
and closed the doors and you're all alone

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.543
it's like everything closes in on you.

00:03:32.073 --> 00:03:34.870
You have to learn to deal
with yourself a little more.

00:03:37.071 --> 00:03:38.553
- And how do you support yourself?

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.080
Or how have you supported
yourself over the years?

00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:46.880
When I first met you I think
you were dating guys, right?

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:47.863
- Yeah.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:50.380
- Do you still do that?

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.213
- What was that?

00:03:51.213 --> 00:03:52.070
- You still do that?

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:52.903
- Yeah.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.573
Dating?

00:03:54.573 --> 00:03:55.406
- Yeah.

00:03:55.406 --> 00:03:56.350
- No I don't anymore.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.563
I'm on disability for my mental.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.020
- What's your mental condition?

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.570
- I have psychosis and depression,

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:10.730
anorexia and transgender dysphoria.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.530
For some reason they consider
that a disability, I don't

00:04:18.542 --> 00:04:20.517
but I got an SSTI in 2013

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.970
which has been been a big
blessing because you can't depend

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.040
on nobody out here

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.040
You gotta find the hussle yourself.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.420
And me coming from a small town,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.183
it was a big culture shock.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.550
Cause everything is so
busy and it's so fast

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.550
and I'm just standing there
dumbfounded on everything.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.180
- Have you had bad things
happen to you here?

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.860
Being transgender do you get picked out?

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.763
- Yes a lot.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.360
But the whole overall majority

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.360
is very more just well welcoming of it.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.770
- It's more accepted here right?

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:08.820
- Yeah, exactly.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.883
- Than it would be in Indiana.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:14.660
- Very different.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.830
I was in shock.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.370
I mean, people don't even blink an eye

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.430
and just call you she

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.823
and it's a big shock from where I'm from.

00:05:22.888 --> 00:05:25.930
You had to pry their teeth
out to let them know,

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.230
look, this ain't cool but

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.360
you still have to watch
your back out here.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.273
There's a lot of deceiving
people, which is scary because I

00:05:39.917 --> 00:05:43.633
had to learn the hard way
how deceiving people can be.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.270
I'm not saying they're bad people, but

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:50.823
there's a survival program out here.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.320
You just gotta learn to respect everybody

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.680
and keep on your side of
the road and keep pushing

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.610
and usually it's pretty cool.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:05.080
- What's been the most
important lesson you've learned

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.630
since you came out to California

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.890
- Improvising.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.550
And even though sometimes
people don't act like

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:20.170
the community's important because

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:23.173
as a whole is what makes us Skid Row.

00:06:24.582 --> 00:06:26.920
But a lot of times we push
through every day just

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.433
trying to make it and not realizing that.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.320
But when it comes down
to it, there's usually

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.497
somebody you can depend on
to get through something.

00:06:39.252 --> 00:06:40.353
- And do you have friends?

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.823
- Yeah a few in my housing.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.150
Like I said it's been a big adjustment.

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:56.143
I think I have a big trust
issue with a lot of people.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.120
So my mind wants to be,
you want to be, you know

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.860
living this fantasy life

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.633
but your mind keeps telling
you something different.

00:07:09.223 --> 00:07:10.140
It's kind of hard.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.980
- You still have contact with your family?

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:16.160
- Somewhat. I haven't
been lately, but I was

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.430
the majority of the time
I've been down here.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.230
- How was your relationship with them?

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:22.140
Were your parents accepting of you?

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.710
- They tried, but it was hard for them.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.993
It was part of the reason
why I came down here.

00:07:30.827 --> 00:07:34.330
But I had to learn that it's not all them,

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.090
because we're always
stuck in our own feelings

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.450
that we don't recognize that

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:46.160
hey, these people gave
birth to something and now

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.610
that person's grown a little
bit and is telling them

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.010
they're something different
and that's hard for-

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:52.990
We don't realize that because we're going

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.040
through it ourselves.

00:07:58.672 --> 00:08:00.540
So they're hard.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.210
They're both sides of the spectrum.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.870
One's a biker hillbilly
from Kentucky and the other

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.493
one's a Catholic city girl.

00:08:10.311 --> 00:08:13.280
So surprisingly they tried but it was hard

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:17.020
for them to accept because
they're so old school.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.940
- Are drugs, a part of your life?

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:23.880
- Not at the beginning

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.472
because I was a real bad
alcoholic when I came out here

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:28.305
and then I was sober.

00:08:28.305 --> 00:08:31.060
But in the last two years, yes.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.870
- You started using what?

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:33.703
- Meth.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:37.100
It's just kind of out on a limb.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.720
I just started using it.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:43.720
And it's just been a pretty
bad habit ever since.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.920
- Well, what does crystal meth do for you?

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:50.990
- Honestly as a social
thing, because I've always

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:54.483
been so introverted and
kind of hurted it over that.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.210
Another thing about Skid
Row is there's always

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:04.790
so many sides of a whole
big spectrum, a variety

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:09.790
of people, but the most of
us have an issue that's been

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.720
pointed out or labeled.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.930
And, but it that's, what's
great about Skid Row is

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.850
it's a variety and it
doesn't matter who you are.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:26.580
You'll be, you'll fit in some kind of-

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.467
- There there's everything here.

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:32.186
You've got gang members,
you've got transgenders,

00:09:32.186 --> 00:09:34.860
you've got sex workers,
you've got drug addicts.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.453
- It's vernic to everything.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.690
- Pedophiles.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:43.200
- Yeah, virtually.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.470
- Murders.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.453
- Yeah. You got to watch all that.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:52.830
That's why kind of like
a network, almost people

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.930
that you know, you kind
of have to stick together

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:59.610
with that kind of thing
to let each other in

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:02.523
on a heads up on who's
the next new person or.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.840
- What's been the hardest
part of your life?

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:06.955
- Hardest part?

00:10:06.955 --> 00:10:08.590
- Yeah.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.686
- When you're at home with your family

00:10:10.686 --> 00:10:11.953
or since you've been on the street?

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.980
- I believe actually

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.850
the street has not been as bad

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.320
as say preteens and teens.

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:24.640
- It must've been a hard time.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.330
- And right after, cause I wasn't much

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.640
aware of being trans, or what trans was.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.090
I just knew what I was going through.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:38.090
And so it was hard for me to
adjust and grow in that aspect

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:43.320
until I came out here and
just came out here and it just

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.340
kinda just happened just
by living it instead of

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.510
out constantly pondering or being-

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:50.360
- What was the best time of your life?

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.193
- Best time?

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:57.653
Coming out here, to Skid Row.

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:05.893
It was the worst situation but
best change and best growth

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:11.743
that I've ever, and glimmer
of hope that I've ever seen.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.400
I guess we all reach first a
star but some of us don't seem

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:23.410
to be able to even have
a hand close to it.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:27.020
And the closest I came to
one coming out of here.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:27.853
- Interesting.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:30.610
What kind of things have you seen

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.383
since you've been out here in Skid Row?

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:35.156
- Oh, a lot.

00:11:35.156 --> 00:11:37.566
- Or can you give me an example?

00:11:37.566 --> 00:11:38.860
- That's the hardest thing

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:41.480
in the world is I have
to turn the other cheek

00:11:42.649 --> 00:11:46.893
when you want to stand up
or stick up for somebody.

00:11:46.893 --> 00:11:51.893
I've seen a trans female
to male lesbian be beat up

00:12:00.627 --> 00:12:02.620
and I couldn't do anything about it.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.550
I saw her like months later and she said

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.760
it's a good thing you didn't cause,

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.170
she's stubborn apparently.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:11.280
And she didn't want to
move out of her spot.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.323
And she stood up for herself,

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:19.013
like I guess like six
eight people beat her.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:28.690
I've seen tent hoppers, so
they call, tent hoppers.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.830
There's so many things.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.280
- But what's a, what's a tent hopper.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:42.300
- Just a female that hops tent to tent

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:46.280
for supplies or whatever to-

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.113
- Drugs?

00:12:47.113 --> 00:12:50.300
- Yeah. Drugs. Just to
have a place to stay

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:54.073
or get cleaned up or just simple stuff.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:02.330
It saddens me because one I'm nosy but two

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.030
I can't see going that low.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:08.100
I think what we have to share

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.560
with somebody in that
intimacy is a little bit

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.210
wears a whole lot more than that.

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:19.490
But I seen all kinds of stuff.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.720
You know, seen people stabbed,

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:23.833
seen people jump off the roof.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:30.380
I just recently had a friend
that jumped off the roof,

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.550
well not the roof, the
railing in my building.

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:33.890
He was a close friend of mine.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.660
He was supposed to be
there meeting me actually

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.303
and he died instantly.

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:45.420
Some people like their
minds get so full of stuff

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.943
I think they can't take it anymore.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.280
I've came really close to it, I believe.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:55.110
But I just don't have the total guts to go

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.163
to a hundred percent.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:00.053
I don't know.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.840
- What do you think the biggest issue is

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:05.750
for all these people down here?

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:06.710
Would you say it's drugs?

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.300
Would you say it's mental
health, what would you say?

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.230
- It's a variety.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.820
I think a lot come down here

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.797
because of the resources,
and kind of get stuck.

00:14:16.897 --> 00:14:18.020
A lot of them-

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.230
- Freedom and the lack of
responsibility and all that?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:21.063
- Yeah exactly.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:27.510
Complacent. A lot is mental
illness I believe and the drugs.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.563
And like you said, the easy life.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.830
A lot like me, come down here

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:37.463
and they find a common
ground for themselves.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:42.980
It's hard to say how that happens
or what I'm talking about.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.670
But like when I came
out here, I didn't have,

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:50.670
I was so oppressed, you
know, by family by my past

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:52.810
and we came out here

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:57.810
and I found a more foundation for myself.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.480
I came more in lined,
when people used to say

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:07.410
that I had no awareness
what they meant, but I was

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.210
I became more aligned

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:13.273
and that's very significant
personally to one person.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:19.883
It gives you that freedom,
majority of the time.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.900
- Where do you see your
life going from here?

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.140
- Coming from here?

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:30.500
I used his say being a star

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:35.500
but reality is we don't
know how that will work.

00:15:40.994 --> 00:15:43.700
- When you say be a star and
you're hoping to be an actor?

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.223
- I came out here to dance.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:50.483
Then I started looking
for extras, extra work,

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:58.340
some kind of gig, maybe modeling or dance

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.520
or acting like you said

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.320
- How old are you now?

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:05.600
- I'm 29.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:06.433
- You're what?

00:16:06.433 --> 00:16:07.266
- 29.

00:16:10.909 --> 00:16:11.742
And you?

00:16:14.192 --> 00:16:18.192
- I think I'm old enough
to be your grandfather.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.990
- What are your goals at
this point in your life?

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.133
Do you have a goal

00:16:26.133 --> 00:16:28.261
or are you just trying
to survive at this point?

00:16:28.261 --> 00:16:29.094
- That's the problem.

00:16:29.094 --> 00:16:33.440
The last two years the things
I've been through with people

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:38.440
and spiritually, my drive is not there.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:43.520
The mindset, but the drive
is kind of like depleted

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:48.600
and actually I've met a new man.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.660
I was with one for nine years,

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:53.710
but that didn't work out and he's

00:16:57.270 --> 00:17:00.410
I want to say wishy-washy
but it's not wishy-washy.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.620
He's like me, kinda like keeps a wall up

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:10.440
but I didn't expect expectations
to grow, but now I do.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.373
I expect something hopefully with him.

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.240
We all want to be rich.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:22.503
I want to be able to live
somewhat of a lavish life someday.

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:24.840
Cause I've never had that.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:29.463
- All right, J.

00:17:29.463 --> 00:17:30.340
It's nice seeing you again.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:32.060
Thank you for talking with me

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:34.920
and good luck with wherever
your life goes from here.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:35.753
- Thank you.

